A practical simulator for childcare workers and parents.

Place 3D rock, scissors, and paper hands on the screen to try snails, flowers, free-form shapes, and more—before you craft with paper or real hands. Great for lesson prep, play ideas, and exploring shapes with kids.

【When to use it】
・Planning rock-paper-scissors crafts or games for childcare
・Trying poses and shapes together with children
・Simulating layouts on screen before arranging paper or props

【What you can do】
・Add rock / scissors / paper and place them freely
・Move, rotate, and resize hands
・Save works and manage a gallery
・Share creations as images

Easy to try and rearrange, so it helps with classroom prep and parent–child play ideas. Explore many patterns right on your screen.
